-- title:
--   Retained ideals equal ideals locally generated by normalized polynomial sections
-- statement:
--   Let $I$ be a multihomogeneous polynomial ideal containing the defining ideal of the embedded group. Its retention at all genuine homogeneous representatives equals the ideal locally generated by its normalized polynomial sections at translation zero. Local generation is the existing definition using finite sums with regular rational coefficients on actual Zariski neighborhoods. Each coefficient is a ratio of homogeneous polynomials of the same degree. Both sides are actual ideals, including their multiplicities. The proof supplies the algebraic denominator clearing and local-to-global comparison required in Definition 4.2 and the proof of Proposition 4.3. No completeness or algebraic closedness assumption is needed.
-- source:
--   Philippon (1986), Lemmes de zéros dans les groupes algébriques commutatifs, Definition 4.2 and Proposition 4.3, printed pp. 373–374; https://numdam.org/articles/10.24033/bsmf.2060/ .

import Definitions.Def_PhilipponMultiplicity_SectionFour
import Definitions.Def_PhilipponMultiplicity_SectionThreeSupport
set_option autoImplicit false
open scoped BigOperators Topology
open PhilipponMultiplicity

theorem PhilipponMultiplicity.retained_ideal_eq_locally_generated_sections
    (K : Type*) [NontriviallyNormedField K] (G : EmbeddedGroupProduct K)
    (I : Ideal G.CoordinateRing) (hI : IsMultihomogeneousIdeal G.ambient I)
    (hG : G.vanishingIdeal Set.univ ≤ I) :
    retainOnGroup G I = translatedIdeal G 0 I := by sorry
